Tonight's problem:  Delay eager clients until the servers
  have settled on a common cachepath.  Currently, there's
  a race that occasionally results in clients making file
  requests early and getting an uninitialized cacahepath.

Moving the client socket initialization out of the server
  initialization code result in the server are-you-alive
  message failing to get through.

Net approach:  Allow the clients to connect, but send back
  a NOT_YET response until the cachepath is sorted.

